note Exercism-style exercise "change": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/change
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note findfewestcoins writes the fewest coins from the denominations coins (each usable any number
note of times) that add up to target (at most 1000) into o, in ascending order, and returns how many;
note or -1 when target cannot be made, -2 when target is negative.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/change
om2
fn findfewestcoins coins view ulong * target long o edit ulong * to long
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
